replies.text:
@RepJoshG This reads like DC 101: patch now, promises later—and “pay-fors not yet scored.”

If subsidies are expiring, pass a clean temporary bridge. Then deliver real reform: rein in hospital markups, fix PBM rebate/fee games, and expose payer/Medicare contract algorithms that inflate bills far beyond retail.

Bring bill text, scored offsets, and enforcement.

Or is it business as usual—ignoring those who pay the price and protecting DC backroom deals?

@SenBillCassidy @LeaderJohnThune @NoLabelsOrg
